  "erdos": 673,
  "title": "What is the typical growth of the sum of ratios of consecutive ordered divisors of an integer?",
  "scope": "For G(n), the sum of each positive divisor divided by its next larger divisor, every fixed real threshold is exceeded on a set of natural density one. The ordinary summatory function over 1<=n<=X is asymptotic to X log X with leading constant 1 along natural X, and the average (1/X) times the sum over 1<=n<=X tends to infinity.",
  "attribution": "Existing plby/lean-proofs source. The primary E673 header credits Paul Erdos and Gerald Tenenbaum for the informal result, and Codex / GPT-5.6 Sol for formalization; original spellings and accents are preserved in the copied header. Imported E459 credits Stijn Cambie for its informal result and Aristotle / Boris Alexeev / Wouter van Doorn for its formalization. Util.Density preserves its Formal Conjectures Authors copyright and modification notice. All 12 source notices remain byte-for-byte intact; these dependency credits are not reassigned as primary E673 authorship. No uploader-as-original-author, priority or recipient claim.",
